  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "All strings in Chefland are beautiful because they are binary strings (a binary string contains only characters '0' and '1'). The beauty of a binary string SSS is defined as the number of pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) (1≤i≤j≤∣S∣1 \\le i \\le j \\le |S|1≤i≤j≤∣S∣) such that the substring Si,Si+1,…,SjS_i, S_{i+1}, \\ldots, S_jSi​,Si+1​,…,Sj​ is special.\n\nFor a binary string UUU, let's denote the number of occurrences of the characters '1' and '0' in UUU by cnt1cnt_1cnt1​ and cnt0cnt_0cnt0​ respectively; then, UUU is special if cnt0=cnt1⋅cnt1cnt_0 = cnt_1 \\cdot cnt_1cnt0​=cnt1​⋅cnt1​.\n\nToday, Chef's friend Araspa is celebrating her birthday. Chef wants to give Araspa the most beautiful binary string he can find. Currently, he is checking out binary strings in a shop, but he needs your help to calculate their beauties. Tell Chef the beauty of each binary string he gives you.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤∣S∣≤1051 \\le |S| \\le 10^51≤∣S∣≤105",
      "each character of SSS is '0' or '1'"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single string SSS.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the beauty of the string SSS.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n010001\n10",
        "output": "4\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: The special substrings correspond to (i,j)=(1,2),(1,6),(2,3),(5,6)(i, j) = (1, 2), (1, 6), (2, 3), (5, 6)(i,j)=(1,2),(1,6),(2,3),(5,6)."
      }
    ]
  },
